        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e81bbd04-0a7f-50aa-b570-9c4eba3b5e5d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Ghana, Burkina Faso, Ivory Coast, Togo, Elubo, Sekondi-Takoradi, Cape Coast, Winneba, Accra, Tema, Aflao, Dissin, Ioba\n- Systems: N1, National Highway 1\n- Events: Fancy Dress Festival, Kakamotobi\n- Topics: fishing ports, masquerade festivals, transport routes\n\nFacts:\n- The N1, or National Highway 1, is a national highway in Ghana that begins at Elubo on the Ivory Coast border and ends at Aflao on the Togo border.\n- The N1 passes through Sekondi-Takoradi, Cape Coast, Winneba, Accra, and Tema in Ghana.\n- Winneba, traditionally known as Simpa, is a historic fishing port on the south coast of Ghana.\n- Winneba lies 90 miles east of Cape Coast.\n- The Fancy Dress Festival, locally called Kakamotobi, is a masquerade festival celebrated annually in Winneba in Ghana's Central Region from Christmas to January 1.\n- Dissin is a town in Burkina Faso near the northwest corner of Ghana.\n- Dissin is the seat of the Dissin Department in Ioba Province.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
